+NOMROM 1.10.5+26 — TorBox collection file selection and local diagnostics
+Copyright (c) Mark Mateo. Distributed under the repository's MIT license.
+
+WHY THIS UPDATE EXISTS
+
+Fresh MiNERVA selections still failed with FILE_NOT_FOUND in 1.10.4. Review
+reproduced a compatibility gap: strict path matching rejected a catalog file
+when TorBox used a different enclosing folder, even if the filename matched.
+The affected account's actual TorBox response has not been captured, so this
+reproduction is not proof that it explains every reported failure.
+
+FILE SELECTION
+
+The resolver can read an optional proof from the existing local catalog. It
+requires a valid torrent hash, a complete contiguous member index, consistent
+duplicate rows, safe relative paths, bounded nonnegative sizes, and an exact
+selected index/path/positive-size tuple. Raw filename/size uniqueness and
+once-decoded filename/size uniqueness are checked separately. The lookup uses
+the existing torrent_infohash index, has a three-second wait limit, and makes
+no extra account or network request. No proof is cached across catalog updates.
+
+TorBox's ordinary path matching remains available. When that cannot find a
+file, the new filename fallback requires a proof bound to the exact request,
+the complete provider file count, unique valid provider IDs, matching summed
+file bytes and top-level torrent bytes, and an exact unique filename and size.
+Conflicting name and short_name basenames do not qualify for this fallback.
+The provider's file ID is used to request the link. Catalog array positions,
+the torrent's display name and backend download paths are not file identities.
+
+Literal paths and filenames are preferred before the once-decoded pass.
+Literal plus signs remain plus signs. Malformed percent escapes remain literal
+for matching; both Dart exception forms are handled. Pause, cancellation and
+credential changes suppress late results across the optional catalog lookup.
+
+COPY DETAILS
+
+Failed TorBox file-selection and download-link requests can carry a small,
+local diagnostic report. Downloads exposes a Copy details icon when this
+report is available. Copying does not upload, retry, or start a download.
+
+The report includes the app version, failure stage/code, selected relative
+catalog path, expected bytes, file/readiness counts, collection checks and up
+to five relevant file basenames with sizes and the provider's zipped flag.
+It omits provider directories, account/torrent IDs, URLs, magnets, raw response
+bodies and credentials. The current request's credential is removed before
+details reach task storage; malformed/encoded text fails closed for privacy.
+Both storage and copied reports are bounded to 4 KiB. A versioned envelope
+uses the existing error database column; legacy plain errors remain readable.
+Retries, cancellation and unrelated failures clear stale details. Existing
+Waiting for debrid / Check again behavior from 1.10.4 is preserved.
+
+VERIFICATION AND LIMITS
+
+Focused fixtures cover changed folders, exact revision/size selection,
+ambiguous names, incomplete collections, malformed/duplicate IDs, total-size
+mismatches, encoded/literal filenames, diagnostics redaction and persistence,
+clipboard behavior, and task lifecycle races. Read-only catalog probes cover
+the referenced GameCube, Xbox and New Nintendo 3DS collections. These probes
+validate metadata; no ROM content or authenticated TorBox response was used.
+
+The delivered verification report records the actual Windows analyzer/test,
+release build, installer/portable package, signed-update regression and native
+smoke results. It also records the source snapshot from the same Windows run.
+Live TorBox acceptance and an interactive installer upgrade remain separate
+from those automated checks. If a download still fails, use Downloads → Copy
+details and share the copied report to identify the actual returned file list.
+
+The original updater public configuration, existing database schema,
+Windows features and prior Skraper integration remain in this candidate.
+No replacement publisher public key was supplied. No release or update feed
+is published by building or packaging this candidate.
